<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  THE BYTE-EXACTNESS GATE for proposal 35, channels='2' half (§5, built by B1a).

  This repo has gated render exactness by cmp since the beginning, but only ever
  BETWEEN RUNS — never against a stored file. Proposal 35 rewrites the most
  load-bearing contract in the engine (the frozen page grows a channel
  dimension), and its entire safety argument is that the whole mechanical sweep
  happens while every page is still one channel wide, so the byte gate is green
  BY CONSTRUCTION through the riskiest phase. That argument needs a golden that
  outlives the session which produced it. Hence goldens/mc_stereo.wav, committed.

  The fixture project carries one of every path this proposal touches, each in
  its OWN time window so a byte difference names its own culprit by offset:

    0.00-0.60 s   plain clip                 offset 44 .. 115244
    0.65-1.28 s   stretched clip (x1.25)     offset 124844 .. 244844
    1.35-1.95 s   pitched clip (+700 cents)  offset 259244 .. 374444
    2.00-2.60 s   container/asset clip       offset 384044 .. 499244
    2.70-3.30 s   clip on a NESTED lane      offset 518444 .. 633644
    3.35-3.95 s   clip through a twtestclap  offset 643244 .. 758444

  (16-bit stereo PCM, 44-byte header: offset = 44 + frame * 4.)

  It is LOADED into a freshly-new project, never built by a save-load-save round
  trip: §7 trap 10 — load-project deserializes INTO the current project instead
  of replacing it, so a round trip accumulates orphan mixers and chains. Loading
  a fixture into a new project is the shape that is safe.

  Regenerate the .qxp with tests/tools/gen_mc_corpus.qxa. Re-freezing the .wav
  requires an AC that licenses it and a written explanation of why the bytes
  moved (§5).

  TODAY THIS RENDERS THE SAME BYTES AS mc_golden_mono, and that is not a
  mistake in the corpus. RenderSession hard-codes config.channels = 2 and
  duplicates one mono bus into both, so a channels='1' project and a
  channels='2' project produce identical files (M1 made the count DATA ONLY).
  The two goldens are kept apart anyway because B5 is where they must diverge —
  and a corpus that only acquired its second half at the milestone that needs it
  would be re-frozen exactly when the gate was supposed to be holding still.

  DEPENDENCY, stated rather than assumed: the last window needs twtestclap.clap
  next to the binary, i.e. the clap submodule present at configure time. Without
  it the plugin is a Missing placeholder, the insert is transparent, and this
  case fails on the very last window while the other five match — which is a
  correct and legible way for a missing dependency to announce itself.
-->
<SActionScript version="1" name="mc_golden_stereo">

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <load-project path="../goldens/mc_stereo.qxp"/>

    <!-- Pages resident before anything is rendered. Reported, not asserted:
         the count is a function of the readahead and the worker count, so a
         bound would be a flake generator. Making it VISIBLE is the point. -->
    <report-page-memory label="mc_stereo after load"/>

    <render filename="mc_stereo.wav" format="wav" quality="10" durationSec="4.0"/>

    <report-page-memory label="mc_stereo after render"/>

    <!-- THE GATE. -->
    <assert-file-identical actual="mc_stereo.wav" expected="../goldens/mc_stereo.wav"/>

    <!-- Every window carries audio, so a golden that went silent could not pass
         by matching a silent render. These bands are wide on purpose: they are
         a liveness check, not a second exactness gate. -->
    <assert-audio-energy filename="mc_stereo.wav"
                         startFrame="2000" frameCount="24000"
                         minRms="0.05" maxRms="0.60"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="mc_stereo.wav"
                         startFrame="33000" frameCount="24000"
                         minRms="0.05" maxRms="0.60"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="mc_stereo.wav"
                         startFrame="66000" frameCount="24000"
                         minRms="0.05" maxRms="0.60"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="mc_stereo.wav"
                         startFrame="98000" frameCount="24000"
                         minRms="0.05" maxRms="0.60"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="mc_stereo.wav"
                         startFrame="131000" frameCount="24000"
                         minRms="0.05" maxRms="0.60"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="mc_stereo.wav"
                         startFrame="162000" frameCount="24000"
                         minRms="0.02" maxRms="0.60"/>

    <!-- AC B1a.2: THE GATE MUST BE SEEN TO FAIL. A gate that has only ever
         passed is not known to be a gate — and the failure mode this guards
         against is not "the verb is wrong" but "the verb compares the render
         with itself", which passes for ever.

         Muting the plugin track is a deliberate, minimal corruption: it changes
         only the last 0.6 s, so the rejection below also demonstrates that the
         diagnosis LOCATES the difference rather than merely announcing one. The
         warning it prints carries the first differing offset (~643 244, the
         start of the twtestclap window) and the differing-byte count. -->
    <set-track-mute trackPath="5" muted="1"/>
    <render filename="mc_stereo_muted.wav" format="wav" quality="10" durationSec="4.0"/>
    <assert-file-identical actual="mc_stereo_muted.wav"
                           expected="../goldens/mc_stereo.wav"
                           expectReject="true"/>

    <!-- …and back. This is not decoration: it says the difference above was the
         mute and not an unrelated drift, and it exercises invalidation across
         the gate rather than only in one direction. -->
    <undo count="1"/>
    <render filename="mc_stereo_unmuted.wav" format="wav" quality="10" durationSec="4.0"/>
    <assert-file-identical actual="mc_stereo_unmuted.wav"
                           expected="../goldens/mc_stereo.wav"/>

    <report-page-memory label="mc_stereo after three renders"/>
  </actions>

  <assertions>
    <!-- plain, stretched, pitched, asset, folder (holding the nested lane), fx -->
    <assert-track-count equals="6"/>
  </assertions>

</SActionScript>
